From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?S=C3=A9bastien=20Celles?= <s.celles@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 6 Jun 2026 10:38:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/62] feat(verimark): wire all 8 vfuncs
 (list/delete/verify/identify/enroll)

Adds the libfprint vfunc implementations for the Kensington VeriMark DT
on top of the existing TLS-PSK handshake / session pre-integration:

- list:     0x9f 01 returns FpPrint array carrying class-1 storage_handle
- delete:   0xa3 (cascading 3-class delete confirmed runtime)
- verify:   capture pipeline (0x39 RICH / 0x86 frame_ready_arm /
            structured 0x80 / poll 0x87 / 0x39 SPARSE / 0x81)
            + 0x99 simple match + 0xa0 02 resolver class-2 to class-1
            for strict per-print verification
- identify: same pipeline + gallery search by resolved storage_handle
- enroll:   12-opcode prelude, 0x96 01 begin, per-swipe WARM-mode capture
            with RICH/SPARSE LED keep-alive and pre-cycle drain,
            bitmask-gated 7-stage progress, 0x96 03 commit, 0x9e refresh,
            0x96 04 finish (template attached to user-supplied FpPrint)

New wrappers:
- capture.{h,c}: 0x19 init, structured 0x80 capture_start, 0x86 event_config
                 with 128-bit masks (LE), 0x87 event_read returning parsed
                 event records with frame-ready helper
- match.{h,c}: simple 0x99 flag-only call returning the 175-byte verdict
- storage.{h,c}: 0xa3 delete_object, 0xa0 02 resolve_template_to_handle
- enroll.{h,c}: new module wrapping 0x96 sub-commands 01/02/03/04 with
                the 80-byte add_image response parser (bitmask, verdict,
                swipe index, cumulative quality)

All 8 vfuncs runtime-validated against a real 047d:00f2 sensor.

Test suite: 10 meson suites, 94 tests green (proto, crypto, tls, pairing,
session, handshake, storage, capture, match, enroll). New TDD coverage
for every wrapper added in this commit.

Known limitations (follow-ups):
- Synchronous implementation throughout; upstream merge requires fpi_ssm
  refactor.
- Single-attempt verify/identify; on-chip pre-filter rejects ~50% of
  touches without the retry loop the Python reference uses (3 attempts,
  WARM mode on retry).
- Red-LED no-match feedback not deterministic; exact 0x39 payload-to-LED
  mapping not formally reversed yet.
- TOFU dual-OS: a sensor paired under Linux must be re-paired to keep
  Windows Hello working (no host-side unpair opcode exists).

Drafted with AI assistance.
