+/**
+ * Build an FpPrint that carries a single device-side tuid as opaque
+ * driver data. The libfprint convention for MoC drivers (cf.
+ * goodixmoc `fp_print_from_template`) : `fpi-data` is a GVariant
+ * tuple whose first element is a byte array containing the device-
+ * side identifier. The matching/delete paths read that identifier
+ * back to drive the wire opcode.
